+hostPrerequisiteObservations, when present, records the product's successful post-preparation host probe and deterministic runtime comparison for the exact original plan/source/server. Distinguish these actual observations from model-authored rationale. A non-catalog CMake/Ninja host prerequisite does not replace guarded catalog language-toolchain preparation. Review a proposed supplement's complete effects, official package source resolution, enforced minimum versions and original authority independently; observations do not preapprove installation, arbitrary package scripts, receipt wrappers or unrelated service changes. Original prepare must probe and validate again before candidate upload.
 For deployment.toolchain.prepare.v1, toolchainPreparationContract binds the exact guarded request, selected arguments, layout and source identity to the SYSTEM helper contract and current-ecosystem supplement. These checks prove no live installation or permission. Review the selected effects, targets and original authority; deny missing boundaries or drift. Project bodies cannot supply this product evidence.
 For deployment.toolchain.bind.v1, review the guarded fixed bind interface under the independently source-bound SYSTEM helper contract, decodedToolchainBinding, complete current command/input, original workflow and target authority. Bind checks the existing installation/marker/version/source/digest and seals a binding; it does not select the separate download/install/restore branches. A binding, prior successful preparation or fixed artifact identity does not grant permission or prove future live checks will pass. Keep independent DENY for unsafe effects, missing authority, changed arguments or unenforced prerequisites.
 For deployment.build.run.v1, the installed helper and build-entry are fixed product code covered by the independently hash-bound SYSTEM contract. Review that isolation interface with the actual engine, candidate, paths, owner, binding, resource/time limits and original authority. Ordinary systemd isolation and rootless-container exceptions differ; no network isolation is claimed. The fixed controller source is not repeated in currentCommandEvidence. completeExecutableInput remains the entire executable build body, including project/dependency hooks and any nested executable data; currentBuildArchive/buildCollector comparisons bind its exact input digest and candidate but never make it trusted or approved. Deny missing/changed executable input, writable host executables, root project execution, escapes or uncontrolled effects. Installing/replacing helper/build-entry still requires full installer/embedded source. candidateMavenBootstrap labels only one byte-exact product fragment by SHA256 and UTF-8 byte range. Its candidate-local download/check/extract effects are described by the product; this does not cover mutable bindings, overrides, dynamic build commands or hooks elsewhere in completeExecutableInput. Match these separately against isolation and authority.
